      "verdict": "partial",
      "gap": "Merin p.268 asserts that for mutually relevant A,B, A may be more strongly relevant to B than B to A under one measure, LESS relevant under another, and equally relevant under a third. The route exhibits only 'more' (D: rationality-4-3.tex 238-243, annex rationality-4-3.tex 91-100; p15-024 thm:p15-w02b-p15-024-axiom-status item 3) and 'equal' (Q). Every route measure analysed for the pair comparison (D, L, KO, Z) favours the less probable source, and no measure (e.g. the difference P(E|H)-P(E) of thm:p15-w02b-p15-024-z-characterization item 3) is shown to give the reverse; nor is the claim given a standing in the proofboundary def:p15-w02b-p15-024-dependents (p15-024 lines 947-1032). Supply a worked pair and measure realizing the 'less' case, or account for the claim's standing.",
